6.2 Component Specifications

6.2.1 Cognitive Extractor

Input: Trained agent A = (K_A, D_A, \theta_A).

Output: Set of candidate MTCUs \{c_1, \ldots, c_n\}.

Method: Module partitioning via spectral clustering on computational graph + causal ablation validation.

Pre-registration requirement: Extraction criteria (clustering algorithm, distance metric, ablation threshold) must be specified before examining offspring results.

6.2.2 Compatibility Layer

Input: Two MTCUs c_A, c_B.

Output: \Gamma(c_A, c_B) \in [0,1] and binary compatibility decision.

Method: Interface type-checking + semantic alignment via representational similarity analysis.

6.2.3 Recombination Module

Input: Two compatible MTCUs c_A, c_B and operator set \xi.

Output: Candidate genome G_X^*.

Method: Module selection + graph composition + interface adaptation + representation alignment.

6.2.4 External Validator

Input: Candidate genome G_X^*.

Output: Validation vector (V_1, \ldots, V_7) \in \{0,1\}^7.

Method: Seven-stage pipeline with independent governance.

Independence requirement: Validator must not be modifiable by the evolutionary system.

6.2.5 Frozen Evaluator

Input: Genome G_X.

Output: Trait vector T(X_0).

Method: Instantiate G_X, evaluate on held-out tasks before any G_L-driven update.

6.2.6 Post-Learning Evaluator

Input: Genome G_X, learning mechanism G_L, time horizon t.

Output: Trait vector T(X_t).

Method: Instantiate G_X, run G_L for t steps, evaluate on held-out tasks.

