PART III: ALGORITHMS

8. Algorithm 1: Cognitive Extraction

Input: Trained agent A, target trait T, extraction criteria \mathcal{C}_{\text{ext}}.

Output: Locally minimal MTCU c producing T.

```
Algorithm 1: Cognitive Extraction
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Require: Agent A, trait T, extraction criteria C_ext
Ensure: Locally minimal MTCU c

1:  G_comp ← ComputationalGraph(A)
2:  P ← SpectralClustering(G_comp, C_ext.distance_metric)
3:  candidates ← ∅
4:  for each cluster C_i ∈ P do
5:      c_i ← BuildMTCU(C_i, C_ext.interface_spec)
6:      if Valid(c_i, T) then
7:          candidates ← candidates ∪ {c_i}
8:      end if
9:  end for
10: c ← argmin_{c_i ∈ candidates} |c_i|
11: // Local minimality check
12: for each c' ∈ Ablate_1(c) do
13:     if Valid(c', T) then
14:         c ← c'  // Remove redundant component
15:         goto 11
16:     end if
17: end for
18: return c
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
```

Pre-registration requirement: \mathcal{C}_{\text{ext}} must be specified and logged before any offspring evaluation. The extraction procedure must not access offspring data.

