10. Algorithm 3: Cognitive Recombination

Input: Parent genomes G_A, G_B, operator set \xi, compatibility threshold \tau.

Output: Candidate genome G_X^* or \varnothing.

```
Algorithm 3: Cognitive Recombination
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Require: Genomes G_A, G_B, operators ξ, threshold τ
Ensure: G_X* or ∅

1:  // Extract MTCUs from each parent
2:  c_A ← Extract(G_A)
3:  c_B ← Extract(G_B)

4:  // Check compatibility
5:  Γ ← Compatibility(c_A, c_B)
6:  if Γ < τ then return ∅

7:  // Module selection
8:  M_sel ← SelectModules(c_A, c_B, ξ)

9:  // Graph composition
10: G_graph ← ComposeGraphs(M_sel, ξ)

11: // Interface adaptation
12: G_iface ← AdaptInterfaces(G_graph, ξ)

13: // Representation alignment
14: G_repr ← AlignRepresentations(G_iface, ξ)

15: // Constraint intersection
16: G_constraints ← IntersectConstraints(c_A, c_B)

17: // Assemble candidate genome
18: G_X* ← AssembleGenome(G_graph, G_repr, G_constraints)

19: return G_X*
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
```

