PART IV: MINIMAL PILOT PROTOCOL

16. Pilot Design

16.1 Overview

The pilot is deliberately small-scale. Its purpose is to distinguish cognitive inheritance from six confounds:

\text{cognitive inheritance} \quad \text{vs.} \quad \begin{cases} \text{knowledge transfer} \\ \text{parameter transfer} \\ \text{ordinary program composition} \\ \text{shared-pretraining leakage} \\ \text{extractor artifacts} \\ \text{developmental convergence} \end{cases}

16.2 Materials

Parent A: Small model (1–7B parameters) fine-tuned from base model B_A on arithmetic-reasoning-style tasks D_A, with emphasis on decomposition.

Parent B: Small model (1–7B parameters) fine-tuned from architecturally distinct base model B_B on verification-style tasks D_B (checking solutions, detecting errors).

Critical constraint: B_A \neq B_B (architecturally distinct) to control for subliminal learning. If architecturally distinct models are unavailable, document the shared pretraining corpus explicitly and scope leakage claims accordingly.

Datasets: D_A \cap D_B = \varnothing. Held-out test tasks X_{\text{test}} satisfy X_{\text{test}} \cap D_A = \varnothing and X_{\text{test}} \cap D_B = \varnothing.

16.3 Procedure

```
Pilot Protocol
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PHASE 1: PRE-REGISTRATION
  1.1 Specify extraction criteria C_ext (clustering algorithm,
      distance metric, ablation threshold)
  1.2 Specify evaluation tasks X_test and trait T
  1.3 Specify primary outcome H_0(T) and secondary outcomes
  1.4 Specify control conditions and sample size N
  1.5 Log all specifications with timestamp

PHASE 2: PARENT TRAINING
  2.1 Train Parent A on D_A from base B_A
  2.2 Train Parent B on D_B from base B_B
  2.3 Verify D_A ∩ D_B = ∅
  2.4 Verify B_A ≠ B_B (or document shared pretraining)

PHASE 3: EXTRACTION
  3.1 c_A ← Extract(A, T_decomp, C_ext)
  3.2 c_B ← Extract(B, T_verify, C_ext)
  3.3 c_blind ← ExtractorBlindControl(A, T_decomp, C_ext)
  3.4 Log all extraction results

PHASE 4: RECOMBINATION
  4.1 G_X ← R(c_A, c_B, ξ)
  4.2 G_blind ← R(c_blind, c_B, ξ)
  4.3 Verify V(G_X) = 1 and V(G_blind) = 1

PHASE 5: FROZEN EVALUATION
  5.1 X_0 ← Instantiate(G_X)
  5.2 X_0_blind ← Instantiate(G_blind)
  5.3 T_0 ← EvaluateTrait(X_0, T, X_test)
  5.4 T_0_blind ← EvaluateTrait(X_0_blind, T, X_test)

PHASE 6: CONTROLS
  6.1 Knowledge transfer control: transfer K_A to fresh model
  6.2 Parameter transfer control: transfer θ_A to fresh model
  6.3 Architecture transfer control: transfer G_A to fresh model
  6.4 Random recombination: R(random, random, ξ)
  6.5 Human-designed composition: human-specified G_human
  6.6 Matched germline substitution: Algorithm 6

PHASE 7: POST-LEARNING EVALUATION
  7.1 X_t ← Learn(X_0, G_L, t)
  7.2 T_t ← EvaluateTrait(X_t, T, X_test)

PHASE 8: ANALYSIS
  8.1 Compute H_0(T) with bootstrap CI
  8.2 Compute F_held-out(X_0) vs. controls
  8.3 Compute transgressive fraction
  8.4 Compute extractor artifact check: T_0_blind vs. T_0
  8.5 Compute H_t(T) - H_0(T) for developmental persistence
  8.6 Report all results, including negative results

PHASE 9: PRE-REGISTERED FALSIFICATION
  9.1 If H_0(T) ≈ 0 → AC-DNA unsupported in this domain
  9.2 If H_0(T) > 0 but T_0_blind ≈ T_0 → extractor artifact
  9.3 If H_0(T) > 0 but disappears under shared-pretraining control
      → leakage confound
  9.4 If H_t(T) >> H_0(T) → developmental convergence confound
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
```

