D.2.3 Interface Compatibility

```
TypeCheck(output_type, input_type):
  1: if output_type = input_type then return true
  2: if output_type <: input_type then return true  // Subtyping
  3: if Coercible(output_type, input_type) then return true
  4: return false

Coercible(τ₁, τ₂):
  1: // Check if τ₁ can be coerced to τ₂
  2: if τ₁ = Tensor[Shape₁, DType₁] and τ₂ = Tensor[Shape₂, DType₂] then
  3:     return ShapeCompatible(Shape₁, Shape₂) and DTypeCompatible(DType₁, DType₂)
  4: end if
  5: if τ₁ = Graph[N₁, E₁] and τ₂ = Graph[N₂, E₂] then
  6:     return N₁ <: N₂ and E₁ <: E₂
  7: end if
  8: return false
```

D.3 Invariant Verification

D.3.1 Invariant Classes

Definition D.3.1 (Invariant Classes).

Class Description Example
Structural Preserved by representation Dimensionality, sparsity
Semantic Preserved by meaning Logical consistency
Procedural Preserved by execution Termination, determinism
Relational Preserved across modules Interface contracts
Temporal Preserved over time Stability, convergence

D.3.2 Verification Methods

```
VerifyInvariant(c, inv):
  1: switch inv.class:
  2:     case STRUCTURAL:
  3:         return VerifyStructural(c, inv)
  4:     case SEMANTIC:
  5:         return VerifySemantic(c, inv)
  6:     case PROCEDURAL:
  7:         return VerifyProcedural(c, inv)
  8:     case RELATIONAL:
  9:         return VerifyRelational(c, inv)
 10:     case TEMPORAL:
 11:         return VerifyTemporal(c, inv)
 12: end switch

VerifyStructural(c, inv):
  1: // Check dimensionality
  2: if inv.property = "dimensionality" then
  3:     return CheckDimensionality(c.R, inv.expected)
  4: end if
  5: // Check sparsity
  6: if inv.property = "sparsity" then
  7:     return CheckSparsity(c.R, inv.threshold)
  8: end if
  9: return UNKNOWN

VerifyProcedural(c, inv):
  1: // Check termination
  2: if inv.property = "termination" then
  3:     return CheckTermination(c.Π)
  4: end if
  5: // Check determinism
  6: if inv.property = "determinism" then
  7:     return CheckDeterminism(c.Π)
  8: end if
  9: return UNKNOWN
